---
import LessonLayout from '../../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
---
<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; The Paschal Mystery in the Sacraments" cic="CCC 1135-1209" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What does the word <em>&laquo;Passover&raquo;</em> or <em>&laquo;Pasch&raquo;</em> mean?</li>
<li>How many sacraments are there and what are they?</li>
<li>What does <em>ex opere operato</em> mean?</li>
<li>Which three sacraments imprint a character and why cannot they be repeated?</li>
<li>How is the Passover of Israel related to the Paschal Mystery of Christ?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. What did the word <em>&laquo;sacrament&raquo;</em> mean to you before this class? What does it mean now?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Is there any change in your understanding?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. When were you baptized? Do you know anything about that day?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">If you don't know, ask your parents. If you were baptized as an adult, what was that experience like?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. When did you receive Confirmation? How did you prepare for it?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Do you feel that the Holy Spirit acts in your life?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. In what ways do the sacraments help you in your daily life?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think of one in particular that has been significant.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. How can you live this week more aware that you have <em>&laquo;died and risen with Christ&raquo;</em> in Baptism?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Is there something you need to <em>&laquo;die to&raquo;</em> in order to live more fully?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Read Romans 6:3-11</h4>
<p>Read it slowly three times. The first to understand, the second to feel, the third to pray. Write a phrase that God placed on your heart.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. Research Your Baptism</h4>
<p>Look for your baptismal certificate or ask your parents: when was it, where, who were your godparents? Write down the details and reflect on what that day meant.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Make a Map of the Seven Sacraments</h4>
<p>Draw a central circle with the word <em>&laquo;Passover.&raquo;</em> Around it, the seven sacraments as rays coming from the center. Next to each one, write how you connect it to Christ's Passover.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p><em>&laquo;We were buried therefore with him by baptism into death, so that as Christ was raised from the dead by the glory of the Father, we too might walk in newness of life.&raquo;</em></p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; Romans 6:4</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Christ, Lamb of God,<br />
who by your death conquered death<br />
and by your resurrection gave us life,<br />
thank you for the gift of the sacraments.<br />
May every sacrament I receive<br />
plunge me more deeply into your Passover,<br />
making me die to sin and live for you.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

